course: dictionary
lesson: 1634
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word chief has more than one meaning, so the words around it show you which one to use. In «The Head Chief says Taffy has made a great invention», the chief is the leader of a group, like a tribe.
explain: In «the chief cause of the problem», chief means main. Try the swap: «the main cause of the problem» still makes sense, so chief means main here. Always test your meaning in the sentence.
explain: Chief can also be a friendly word for a man, like «mate» or «boss». «Alright, chief?» is chatty talk, so the people speaking are friends. Clues like who is speaking and how tells you what kind of word it is.
fact: Chief can be a noun (a chief, chiefs) or an adjective (chief).
fact: As a noun, chief means the leader or head of a group, such as a tribe, a police force or an organisation.
fact: As an adjective, chief means most important, main or highest in rank: «the chief reason», «chief executive».
fact: Chief is also an informal word for a man, like «mate» or «boss».
fact: In 1840 many Māori chiefs signed the Treaty of Waitangi with the British Crown.
exercise: «The Head Chief says Taffy has made a great invention.» What does chief mean here? | *The leader of a group | A friendly word for a mate | The most important reason | A cook in a kitchen
exercise: «The chief cause of the problem» is in a formal text. What does chief mean? | A friendly word for a man | Late or delayed | The leader of a tribe | *Most important or main
exercise: Mia says «Alright, chief?» to her friend. What is chief here? | The most important thing | *A friendly word for a man, like mate | The highest rank in an army | The leader of a police force
test: «The Stranger-man thinks the Chief pretended not to notice me.» Which meaning fits best? | A friendly word for a mate | The main reason | A chef who cooks | *The leader of the tribe
test: Which phrase uses chief as an adjective meaning most important? | The chief of the tribe spoke | Alright, chief? | *The chief reason for the trip | The fire chief arrived at the station
exam: Which word could replace chief in «the chief reason» without changing the meaning? | Quietly | Stormy | *Main | Blue
